posts.text:
Starting a place for everyone who keeps jars of bubbling vegetables on the counter. My latest batch of white kimchi:

{{img:kimchi}}

No chilli in this one, so it's gentle and very refreshing.

We had a week of 35 °C, then two days of heavy rain, and now half my tomatoes have split open. Are they still OK to eat?

{{img:tomato}}

(Not mine, mine look much sadder.)

Rode the lakeside loop on Sunday: 62 km, almost flat, quiet roads and a café at the halfway point. The old iron bridge at kilometre 40 is the highlight.

{{img:bridge}}

Go clockwise so you have the wind behind you on the way home.
